// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\stranded-horizons\\docs\\v2\\SELFHOST.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":20,"lines":["+# v2 self-hosting","+","+## Vercel (now)","+- Static frontend deploys as-is: `index.html`, `game.html` (v1), `game-v2.html`, `admin/`.","+- `api/socket.js` is the optional serverless socket shim; set in Vercel env:","+  `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET`, `CORS_ORIGINS` (your Vercel domain), `DATABASE_URL`,","+  `REDIS_URL` (omit Redis for single-instance mode), `DEV_UNAUTHENTICATED=1` only for CI smoke.","+- Set `window.SH_SOCKET_URL` before loading `game-v2.html` if the socket host differs.","+","+## VPS (later)","+1. `cp .env.example .env` and fill `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`, `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET`, `CORS_ORIGINS`.","+2. `docker compose up -d --build`","+3. Apply SQL: `psql $DATABASE_URL -f db/schema.sql`","+4. Point DNS to the VPS, provision TLS (certbot), keep ports closed except 443.","+5. Nightly `pg_dump`; test restores. Postgres + Redis are on the private","+   `internal` network and are never published — only NGINX 443 is public.","+","+## Notes","+- Supabase CLI local stack is dev-only; never expose it. Production uses the compose stack.","+- No managed backups when self-hosting: the operator owns backups, updates, monitoring."]}]}]}
